# FamilyRoots API Sanctuary - Complete Endpoints Directory & Access Guide

## 1. Primary Access Links

### Interactive Swagger UI (OpenAPI Explorer)
You can view, test, and authenticate with all system APIs visually in your browser:
- **Direct Root URL (Auto-Redirects to Swagger)**:
  - Local Development: `http://localhost:5000/` or `http://localhost:3000/`
  - Vercel Deployment: `https://<your-backend-domain>/`
- **Direct Swagger Documentation URLs**:
  - `http://localhost:5000/api/docs` or `https://<your-backend-domain>/api/docs`
  - `http://localhost:5000/docs` or `https://<your-backend-domain>/docs`

### Raw OpenAPI Specifications (For Postman, Insomnia, Code Generators)
- **JSON Specification**: `http://localhost:5000/api/docs-json` or `https://<your-backend-domain>/api/docs-json`
- **YAML Specification**: `http://localhost:5000/api/docs-yaml` or `https://<your-backend-domain>/api/docs-yaml`

### System Health Endpoint
- `http://localhost:5000/health` or `https://<your-backend-domain>/health`

---

## 2. Authentication & Session APIs (`/auth`)

All auth routes can be accessed with either `/auth/...` or `/api/auth/...` prefix.

| Method | Endpoint | Description | Auth Required |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `POST` | `/auth/signup` | Register new user account | Public |
| `POST` | `/auth/signin` | Sign in with email and password (sets HttpOnly cookies) | Public |
| `POST` | `/auth/refresh` | Rotate refresh token and issue new access token | Public (Cookie / Refresh Token) |
| `POST` | `/auth/logout` | Revoke current user session and clear cookies | Bearer JWT / Cookie |
| `POST` | `/auth/logout-all` | Revoke all active devices and sessions for user | Bearer JWT / Cookie |
| `GET` | `/auth/me` | Fetch currently authenticated user profile | Bearer JWT / Cookie |
| `GET` | `/auth/sessions` | List active sessions and device agents | Bearer JWT / Cookie |
| `PATCH` | `/auth/profile` | Update profile information (name, bio, avatar, phone) | Bearer JWT / Cookie |
| `POST` | `/auth/change-password` | Update current user account password | Bearer JWT / Cookie |
| `POST` | `/auth/verify-email` | Verify email token to activate account | Public |
| `POST` | `/auth/resend-verification`| Resend account activation link | Public |
| `POST` | `/auth/forgot-password` | Request password reset token via email | Public |
| `POST` | `/auth/reset-password` | Reset password using one-time token | Public |

---

## 3. Family Sanctuary & Tree Management APIs (`/family`)

All family routes can be accessed with either `/family/...` or `/api/family/...` prefix.

### Sanctuary Overview & Metrics
| Method | Endpoint | Description | Allowed Roles | Permissions |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `GET` | `/family/sanctuary` | Get main family tree overview, stats, and member counts | `OWNER`, `ADMIN`, `SUPER_ADMIN`, `MEMBER`, `USER` | Read-only sanctuary dashboard access |
| `PATCH` | `/family/update` | Update sanctuary family name and description | `OWNER`, `ADMIN`, `SUPER_ADMIN` | Sanctuary core profile management |
| `PATCH` | `/family/settings` | Update sanctuary settings and preferences | `OWNER`, `ADMIN`, `SUPER_ADMIN` | Sanctuary configuration management |
| `GET` | `/family/activity` | Get recent audit activity logs across the sanctuary | `OWNER`, `ADMIN`, `SUPER_ADMIN`, `MEMBER`, `USER` | Read activity feed |
| `GET` | `/family/admin/stats` | Administrative network health and metrics | `ADMIN`, `SUPER_ADMIN` | System platform administration |

### Family Members & Relative Linking
| Method | Endpoint | Description | Allowed Roles | Permissions |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `GET` | `/family/members` | Retrieve all family members in sanctuary | `MEMBER`, `USER`, `OWNER`, `ADMIN`, `SUPER_ADMIN` | Read member directory |
| `GET` | `/family/members/search?q={query}` | Search profiles for deduplication and relative linking | `MEMBER`, `USER`, `OWNER`, `ADMIN`, `SUPER_ADMIN` | Search member profiles |
| `POST` | `/family/members` | Add new relative/member or link existing profile with relationship | `OWNER`, `ADMIN`, `SUPER_ADMIN` (any member), `MEMBER` (relative to self) | Create member & relative links |
| `PATCH` | `/family/members/:id` | Update family member profile details | `OWNER`, `ADMIN`, `SUPER_ADMIN`, or profile owner | Edit member details |
| `DELETE` | `/family/members/:id` | Remove a family member from sanctuary | `OWNER`, `ADMIN`, `SUPER_ADMIN` strictly | Delete member profile (denied for ordinary member) |

### Lineage & Relationships Matrix
| Method | Endpoint | Description | Allowed Roles | Permissions |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `GET` | `/family/relationships` | Get full graph relationship matrix for family tree canvas | `MEMBER`, `USER`, `OWNER`, `ADMIN`, `SUPER_ADMIN` | Read relationship connections |
| `POST` | `/family/relationships` | Create relationship link between two relatives | `OWNER`, `ADMIN`, `SUPER_ADMIN`, `MEMBER`, `USER` | Establish lineage links |

### Memories Vault (With User Isolation)
| Method | Endpoint | Description | Allowed Roles | Permissions |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `GET` | `/family/memories?userId={id}&userEmail={email}` | Retrieve user-isolated family memories gallery | `MEMBER`, `USER`, `OWNER`, `ADMIN`, `SUPER_ADMIN` | Read isolated user memories |
| `GET` | `/family/memories/:id` | Retrieve single memory details | `MEMBER`, `USER`, `OWNER`, `ADMIN`, `SUPER_ADMIN` | Read memory record |
| `POST` | `/family/memories` | Upload new memory story with photos, dates, and locations | `MEMBER`, `USER`, `OWNER`, `ADMIN`, `SUPER_ADMIN` | Create personal memory |
| `PATCH` | `/family/memories/:id` | Update an existing memory | Memory Creator, `OWNER`, `ADMIN`, `SUPER_ADMIN` | Edit memory record |
| `DELETE` | `/family/memories/:id` | Delete memory from vault | Memory Creator, `OWNER`, `ADMIN`, `SUPER_ADMIN` | Delete memory record |

### Events Calendar
| Method | Endpoint | Description | Allowed Roles | Permissions |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `GET` | `/family/events` | List upcoming family reunions, birthdays, and anniversaries | `MEMBER`, `USER`, `OWNER`, `ADMIN`, `SUPER_ADMIN` | Read calendar events |
| `POST` | `/family/events` | Schedule a new family event (virtual or physical) | `OWNER`, `ADMIN`, `SUPER_ADMIN`, `MEMBER`, `USER` | Create calendar event |

### Documents Vault
| Method | Endpoint | Description | Allowed Roles | Permissions |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `GET` | `/family/documents` | Retrieve encrypted document archive | `MEMBER`, `USER`, `OWNER`, `ADMIN`, `SUPER_ADMIN` | Read document files & metadata |
| `POST` | `/family/documents` | Upload single document or files bundle (up to 100MB) | `MEMBER`, `USER`, `OWNER`, `ADMIN`, `SUPER_ADMIN` | Upload document file |
| `POST` | `/family/documents/multiple` | Upload batch documents | `MEMBER`, `USER`, `OWNER`, `ADMIN`, `SUPER_ADMIN` | Upload batch files |
| `DELETE` | `/family/documents/:id` | Delete a single document | Document Uploader, `OWNER`, `ADMIN`, `SUPER_ADMIN` | Delete archive file |
| `DELETE` | `/family/documents` | Purge all documents | `OWNER`, `ADMIN`, `SUPER_ADMIN` strictly | Purge archive vault |

### Invitations & Join Requests
| Method | Endpoint | Description | Allowed Roles | Permissions |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `GET` | `/family/invitations` | Get pending member invitations and requests | `OWNER`, `ADMIN`, `SUPER_ADMIN` | View invitations list |
| `POST` | `/family/invitations` | Send an email invite to join family tree | `OWNER`, `ADMIN`, `SUPER_ADMIN`, `MEMBER`, `USER` | Send join invitation |
| `PATCH` | `/family/invitations/:id` | Accept or reject join request | `OWNER`, `ADMIN`, `SUPER_ADMIN` strictly | Approve/reject admission |

---

## 4. Users Administration APIs (`/users`)

| Method | Endpoint | Description | Allowed Roles | Permissions |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `POST` | `/users` | Create user profile record | `ADMIN`, `SUPER_ADMIN` | System account creation |
| `GET` | `/users` | Retrieve directory of all registered users | `ADMIN`, `SUPER_ADMIN` | User accounts inspection |
| `GET` | `/users/:id` | Find user profile by unique ID | `ADMIN`, `SUPER_ADMIN`, or Account Owner | User details retrieval |
| `PATCH` | `/users/:id` | Update user details or assign role | `ADMIN`, `SUPER_ADMIN`, or Account Owner | Account modification |
| `DELETE` | `/users/:id` | Delete user account | `ADMIN`, `SUPER_ADMIN` strictly | Account termination |

---

## 5. Postman & Curl Example

### Testing Health Status:
```bash
curl -X GET "http://localhost:5000/health"
```

### Testing Sign In:
```bash
curl -X POST "http://localhost:5000/auth/signin" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "email": "owner@familyroots.org",
    "password": "Password123!"
  }'
```

### Downloading OpenAPI Schema into Postman:
Import URL into Postman: `http://localhost:5000/api/docs-json`
